Patch summary:
With every layer client composed (a desktop with an app window: its shadow
and frame force SurfaceFlinger to compose everything itself), hwc3's host
composer had no device layer and flushed SurfaceFlinger's client target to
the display as it was. On virtio-gpu that buffer is guest rendered, and the
host cannot name its layout (gfxstream: "Failed to get info: resource N
missing args"), so crosvm read every frame back and copied it to the console
instead of handing it over as a dma-buf: on an Apple Silicon host the
console's frames cost crosvm a third of a core and scrcpy and ika_stream a
sixth each while a window was open, and nothing at all with none. Now the
client target is composed into the next swapchain image as a single
full-display layer, as a mixed composition is, so the scanout is always a
swapchain image, which gfxstream re-creates with an exportable DRM modifier
when the VMM first exports it. The goldfish (non-virtio-gpu) path still
posts the client target directly. The skip-unchanged-present check already
keys on the client target buffer, so an unchanged picture is still skipped.

